 design"},"207":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/deployment/self-hosted/helm-19","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/deployment/self-hosted/helm#before-you-begin","content":"The chart defaults to a `GatewayClass` named `eg`. Change `gateway.className` if your platform team uses another name."},"208":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/deployment/self-hosted/helm-20","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/deployment/self-hosted/helm#before-you-begin","content":"You provide the PostgreSQL server. The chart's pre-install job connects with the supplied credentials, creates the required `pki`, `authz` and `wfx` databases and service schemas, runs migrations, and applies `services.authz.bootstrap`."},"209":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/deployment/self-hosted/helm-21","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/deployment/self-hosted/helm#before-you-begin","content":"The chart has no Helm dependencies that install PostgreSQL, RabbitMQ, an OIDC provider, Envoy Gateway or cert-manager."},"210":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/deployment/self-hosted/helm-22","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/deployment/self-hosted/helm#1-install-the-gateway-prerequisites","content":"Install or upgrade the Envoy Gateway CRDs before its controller. The commands below match the version used by the Lamassu Helm repository:"},"211":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/deployment/self-hosted/helm-23","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/deployment/self-hosted/helm#1-install-the-gateway-prerequisites","content":"Create the default `GatewayClass` if it does not already exist. Save this manifest as `gateway-class.yaml`:"},"212":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/deployment/self-hosted/helm-24","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/deployment/self-hosted/helm#1-install-the-gateway-prerequisites","content":"Install cert-manager separately before Lamassu. The current chart renders its self-signed issuer and CA certificate resources even when `tls.type: external` makes the Gateway use an existing TLS Secret. Selecting external TLS therefore does not remove the cert-manager prerequisite."},"213":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/deployment/self-hosted/helm-25","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/deployment/self-hosted/helm#2-create-a-values-file","content":"Start with the chart defaults and override the environment-specific values. This example assumes PostgreSQL, RabbitMQ and Keycloak are reachable through Kubernetes DNS, and exposes Keycloak at `/auth` through the shared Lamassu Gateway:"},"214":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/deployment/self-hosted/helm-26","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/deployment/self-hosted/helm#2-create-a-values-file","content":"Do not add `gateway.addresses` by default. Leave address assignment to the load-balancer implementation unless your network design requires a specific Kubernetes-side VIP. The public IP of an upstream NAT gateway or reverse proxy does not belong in this value."},"215":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/deployment/self-hosted/helm-27","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/deployment/self-hosted/helm#2-create-a-values-file","content":"If Keycloak is external and already has its own reachable URL, point the OIDC settings at it and omit the `/auth` entry from `gateway.extraRouting`."},"216":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/deployment/self-hosted/helm-28","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/deployment/self-hosted/helm#tls-with-an-existing-secret","content":"Create a Secret containing `tls.crt` and `tls.key`, then reference it:"},"217":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/deployment/self-hosted/helm-29","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/deployment/self-hosted/helm#provision-the-first-administrator","content":"There is no implicit superuser. Create the role or group expected by `services.authz.bootstrap` in the OIDC provider and assign it to at least one administrator before exposing Lamassu."},"218":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/deployment/self-hosted/helm-30","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/deployment/self-hosted/helm#provision-the-first-administrator","content":"The pre-install and pre-upgrade job applies the bootstrap idempotently: existing principals are preserved and missing grants are added."},"219":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/deployment/self-hosted/helm-31","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/deployment/self-hosted/helm#provision-the-first-administrator","content":"Test both an authorized identity and a denied identity. If no token matches an active bootstrap principal, nobody can administer the PKI."},"220":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/deployment/self-hosted/helm-32","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/deployment/self-hosted/helm#provision-the-first-administrator","content":"See Access control for the principal and policy model."},"221":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/deployment/self-hosted/helm-33","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/deployment/self-hosted/helm#3-install-lamassu","content":"To install a local checkout instead:"},"222":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/deployment/self-hosted/helm-34","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/deployment/self-hosted/helm#4-verify-the-deployment","content":"The Gateway should report `PROGRAMMED=True`. If it is programmed but has no usable address, continue with Expose the Gateway."},"223":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/deployment/self-hosted/helm-35","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/deployment/self-hosted/helm#4-verify-the-deployment","content":"The Helm test checks the CA, DMS Manager, Device Manager and VA health endpoints and verifies the UI response."},"224":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/deployment/self-hosted/helm-36","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/deployment/self-hosted/helm#production-decisions","content":"Before going live, review:"},"225":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/deployment/self-hosted/helm-37","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/deployment/self-hosted/helm#production-decisions","content":"backup and recovery for PostgreSQL and persistent volumes"},"226":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/deployment/self-hosted/helm-38","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/deployment/self-hosted/helm#production-decisions","content":"a production KMS engine; the default filesystem engine is not an HA design"},"227":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/deployment/self-hosted/helm-39","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/deployment/self-hosted/helm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/deployment/self-hosted/helm#production-decisions","content":"shared VA s