ent/troubleshooting-46","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/deployment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/deployment/troubleshooting#a-pod-is-not-ready","content":"an incomplete prior migration."},"416":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/deployment/troubleshooting-47","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/deployment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/deployment/troubleshooting#a-pod-is-not-ready","content":"Generic values request 100 mCPU and 128 MiB and limit to 500 mCPU and 512 MiB. Tune per service when you see OOMKills, throttling or slow startups."},"417":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/deployment/troubleshooting-48","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/deployment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/deployment/troubleshooting#a-pod-is-not-ready","content":"Filesystem-based KMS engines and VA local storage use exclusive-access volumes. Keep a single replica or migrate to shared backends before enabling autoscaling."},"418":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/deployment/troubleshooting-49","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/deployment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/deployment/troubleshooting#a-pod-is-not-ready","content":"Internal calls now fail fast instead of hanging for the clients covered by Egress proxy: connection attempts time out after 30 seconds and TLS handshakes after 10 seconds. The authorization-engine connector keeps its own transport without these dial and handshake timeouts; only its overall 30-second request timeout bounds each call. If an egress proxy handles the cluster's outbound traffic, check the pod's `HTTP_PROXY`, `HTTPS_PROXY` and `NO_PROXY` environment variables and list in-cluster service names in `NO_PROXY`."},"419":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/deployment/troubleshooting-50","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/deployment/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/deployment/troubleshooti