:"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking#qué-ocurre-si-necesitas-tres-gateways","content":"Solo separación lógica; cada listener necesita una tupla única de puerto, protocolo y hostname"},"289":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking-54","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking#qué-ocurre-si-necesitas-tres-gateways","content":"Tres Services `LoadBalancer` independientes no pueden reservar a la vez los mismos puertos 80 y 443 mediante K3s ServiceLB. Usa un Gateway compartido, asigna VIP distintas con otro balanceador o utiliza puertos diferentes."},"290":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking-55","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking#qué-ocurre-si-necesitas-tres-gateways","content":"Envoy Gateway provisiona normalmente un proxy fleet por `Gateway`. Su modo merged Gateway puede compartir un fleet y una dirección, pero no es un cambio directo para varias releases de Lamassu: los listeners generados usan los mismos puertos y protocolos sin hostnames distintos, por lo que entran en conflicto salvo que personalices el diseño."},"291":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking-56","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking#qué-ocurre-si-necesitas-tres-gateways","content":"Usa un front door con SNI solo cuando los Gateways internos deban mantener políticas TLS o mTLS independientes:"},"292":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking-57","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking#qué-ocurre-si-necesitas-tres-gateways","content":"Esto requiere hostnames SNI distintos y configuración de red externa al chart de Lamassu."},"293":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking-58","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking#guía-de-decisión","content":"Si un Gateway puede gestionar TLS y el enrutamiento, usa el valor predeterminado del chart."},"294":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking-59","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking#guía-de-decisión","content":"Si los Gateways necesitan políticas independientes y puedes asignar IP, usa una VIP por Gateway."},"295":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking-60","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking#guía-de-decisión","content":"Si solo necesitas separar los recursos Kubernetes, evalúa merged Gateway y usa tuplas de listener únicas."},"296":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking-61","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking#guía-de-decisión","content":"Si los data planes y la terminación TLS deben ser independientes detrás de una IP, añade un front door con TLS passthrough y SNI."},"297":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking-62","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking#guía-de-decisión","content":"Si nada de lo anterior es posible, usa puertos externos distintos o cambia el diseño de red."},"298":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking-63","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking#proxy-de-salida","content":"Los clientes internos de Lamassu — la conexión con el motor de Vault, las llamadas entre servicios y los webhooks salientes — respetan las variables de entorno `HTTP_PROXY`, `HTTPS_PROXY` y `NO_PROXY`. La excepción es el conector del motor de autorización: usa su propio transporte y no consulta estas variables de proxy. Si tu despliegue enruta el tráfico de salida por un proxy, incluye los nombres de servicio internos del clúster en `NO_PROXY` (por ejemplo `.svc,.cluster.local`) para que el tráfico interno permanezca dentro del clúster. El tráfico de loopback nunca se envía por un proxy."},"299":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking-64","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking#proxy-de-salida","content":"El transporte predeterminado de estos clientes acota el timeout de conexión (30 segundos), el handshake TLS (10 segundos) y la reutilización de conexiones inactivas (90 segundos), de modo que una dependencia inalcanzable falla rápido en lugar de bloquearse; estos valores son los predeterminados del transporte de Go, no configuración de Lamassu. HTTP/2 se negocia cuando el otro extremo lo soporta. El conector del motor de autorización mantiene su propio transporte sin estos timeouts de conexión ni de handshake TLS; solo su timeout global de petición de 30 segundos acota cada llamada."},"300":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking-65","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking#verifica-la-ruta-de-tráfico","content":"Comprueba, en orden:"},"301":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking-66","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking#verifica-la-ruta-de-tráfico","content":"El `Gateway` muestra `Accepted=True` y `Programmed=True`."},"302":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking-67","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking#verifica-la-ruta-de-tráfico","content":"Su estado contiene la dirección esperada."},"303":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking-68","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking#verifica-la-ruta-de-tráfico","content":"El Service `LoadBalancer` generado tiene una dirección externa utilizable."},"304":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking-69","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking#verifica-la-ruta-de-tráfico","content":"El puerto 443 de esa dirección es accesible desde la red del cliente."},"305":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking-70","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking#verifica-la-ruta-de-tráfico","content":"DNS resuelve al endpoint accesible externamente."},"306":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking-71","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking#verifica-la-ruta-de-tráfico","content":"El certificado contiene el nombre DNS o la IP usada por el cliente."},"307":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking-72","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/es/deployment/self-hosted/networking#verifica-la-ruta-de-tráfico","content":"Gateway API trata las direcciones como estado deseado que el controlador puede asignar o rechazar; consulta la introducción a Gateway API para conocer el modelo."},"308":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/es/deployment/self-hosted/overview","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/es/deployment/self-hosted/overview","type":"page","content":"Kubernetes self-managed","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Despliegue","Kubernetes autogestionado"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/es/deployment/self-hosted/overview"},"309":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/es/deployment/self-hosted/overview-0","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/es/deployment/self-hosted/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/es/deployment/self-hosted/overview","content":"Elige un flujo de instalación y una arquitectura de red para Lamassu en tu clúster Kubernetes."},"310":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/es/deployment/self-hosted/overview-1","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/es/deployment/self-hosted/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/es/deployment/self-hosted/overview#despliegue-self-managed-con-kubernetes","content":"Despliegue self-managed con Kubernetes"},"311":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/es/deployment/self-hosted/overview-2","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/es/deployment/self-hosted/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/es/deployment/self-hosted/overview#elige-un-flujo-de-instalación","content":"Elige un flujo de instalación"},"312":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/es/deployment/self-hosted/overview-3","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-41/es/deployment/self-hosted/overvie